{"url": "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/academics/research-postgraduate-programs/overview", "final_url": "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/academics/research-postgraduate-programs/overview", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "MORE ABOUT HKUST\nUNIVERSITY NEWS ACADEMIC DEPARTMENTS A\u2013Z LIFE@HKUST LIBRARY\nMAP & DIRECTIONS JOBS@HKUST FACULTY PROFILES ABOUT HKUST\nSchool of Engineering\nAbout Us\nPeople\nAcademics\nResearch\nNews & Events\nIntranet\nAlumni & Careers\nSupport Us\nResearch Postgraduate Programs\nThe Department offers postgraduate programs leading to the degrees of Master of Science (MSc), Master of Philosophy (MPhil) in Mechnical Engineering, and Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Mechanical Engineering. The programs aim at equipping students with the necessary skills and knowledge to meet the challenges of Hong Kong\u2019s present and future development needs.\nThe MPhil program focuses on strengthening students\u2019 background in mechanical engineering, increasing their mathematical proficiency, and exposing them to the environment of engineering research and development. The PhD program aims at imbuing students with in-depth knowledge of mechanical engineering and the capability of formulating and conducting independent and original research and development in their chosen specialization.\nApplicants for postgraduate programs should have completed a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Engineering or a related field. Qualified applicants may be admitted directly to the PhD program. Students must demonstrate a sufficient command of English in addition to having a basic knowledge of mechanical engineering.\nHong Kong\u2019s industry is in transition and the Department is responding by supporting technology transfer and developing new technologies in the areas of manufacturing, energy, transportation, the environment, and health care. Research also contributes to advances in fundamental knowledge, engineering practice, and technology.\nMechanical Engineering research has six major research foci. These areas are listed below:\nSolid Mechanics and Dynamics\nMaterials Technology\nEnergy Thermal/Fluids and Environmental Engineering\nDesign and Manufacturing Automation\nMicrosystems and Precision Engineering\nAerodynamics and Propulsion\nOverview\nMPhil in Mechanical Engineering\nPhD in Mechanical Engineering\nAdmission\nContact Us\nIntranet\nUseful links\nPrivacy\nSitemap\nCopyright \u00a9 The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology. All rights reserved.\nFollow us on\nFaceBook\nig\nyoutube\nLinkedIn\nEmail", "links": [["University News", "https://www.ust.hk/news"], ["Academic Departments A\u2013Z", "https://www.ust.hk/academics/list"], ["Life@HKUST", "https://www.ust.hk/lifehkust"], ["Library", "http://library.ust.hk/"], ["Map & Directions", "https://www.ust.hk/map-directions"], ["Jobs@HKUST", "https://hkustcareers.hkust.edu.hk/join-us"], ["Faculty Profiles", "https://facultyprofiles.ust.hk/"], ["About HKUST", "https://www.ust.hk/about-hkust"], ["School of Engineering", "https://seng.hkust.edu.hk/"], ["", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/academics/research-postgraduate-programs/overview"], ["", "https://www.ust.hk/zh-hant/"], ["", "https://www.ust.hk/zh-hant/"], ["", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/"], ["", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/"], ["About Us", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/about-us/message-from-acting-head"], ["Message from Head", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/about-us/message-from-head"], ["About MAE", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/about-us/about-mae"], ["Vision and Mission", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/about-us/vision-and-mission"], ["Fast Facts", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/about-us/fast-facts"], ["Quality Assurance", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/about-us/quality-assurance"], ["People", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/people/faculty"], ["Faculty", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/academics/research-postgraduate-programs/overview"], ["Primary Faculty", "https://mae.hkust.edu.hk/en/people/faculty/primary-